A directive on func init is rejected: Go forbids referring to init from anywhere, so an
emitted init() call can never compile, and a package may declare several, each its own
object, so nothing else would catch the duplicate either. Distinct from a set named
init, which is supported, and from a method named init, which is an ordinary selector.
-- config --
import-path: example.com/app
package-name: app
error-is: ErrInitProvider
-- example.com/app/a.go --
package app

type Config struct{}

//plumb:build
func init() {}

//plumb:build
func NewConfig() *Config { return &Config{} }
